[{"id":"484","date":"2026-11-14T01:03:33+00:00","text":"This occasion calls for formal wear. Our 100th Electron is all dressed up, so our pad technicians are too. The launch window for \"The Mountain God Rises\" for QPS Inc opens today: 🚀 6:30pm NZDT 🚀 02:30 pm JST 🚀 05:30 UTC 🚀 12:30 am ET 🚀 9:30 pm PT (Nov 13)","image":"https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/C1o1pEJ1KT565c2m_mgp7vEvenELExNlmJnrwaYgxy-c9FGnjbXEHHLKlN0UmmdSimp1YNybbH9Z5KhIm9o2R5YCLIQX_wlUt_kRGPDDboAsJkd0OvjIPulMBsGgBLddDLKc2Bzc2IYH7ixwWcrJJt_BXOQjenB49Pk-tIU0mmXo3boNKZp0LANzTXQjisvxTdINsNQ0mXmlNoiYSgZ0RSi1G-PctCW4biEnEOI-xK-1zmouhvg9iz0rzuIk-pQKVHTWhJHAjDMfuCOQjYqnnKPIJmJPSOLyzpwS1TQWdgGlxkrSpsg5rHfmBTsNoVE4G1bT-BMQnfcJxUvuuD4exA.jpg","video":"","hasVideo":false},{"id":"483","date":"2026-11-13T22:00:43+00:00","text":"New Zealand is where it all started for Electron - a country with no space heritage. Today, Rocket Lab is a global space company with teams across the United States, Canada, Europe and New Zealand. We're about to launch our 100th rocket.","image":"","video":"","hasVideo":false},{"id":"482","date":"2026-11-13T19:25:54+00:00","text":"To launch a lot of rockets, you need to build a lot of rockets. Our factory is currently producing Electron at a rate of one rocket every 8 days. From single layers of carbon composite, to firing 3D-printed Rutherford engines multiple times before flight - every step requires precision and paranoia. This is Electron's journey from production to the pad.","image":"","video":"","hasVideo":false},{"id":"481","date":"2026-11-13T17:41:01+00:00","text":"Our 100th launch window opens in 12 hours. Join us LIVE for a special broadcast to celebrate this milestone from 04:30 UTC, Saturday November 14th - approximately one hour before lift-off. https://t.co/NGrGy4AhRB","image":"","video":"","hasVideo":false},{"id":"480","date":"2026-11-12T23:37:54+00:00","text":"All eight Rocket Lab-built Lightning platforms for MDA space and Globalstar have passed initial on-orbit functional tests. Orbit raising is now underway, with our team supporting the spacecraft as they climb toward their final orbit.","image":"https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/ddJR9wnbLk6ax3PVKDCShEsxxfwn3yxQ5eC5rBBgruNik6snUhgW5p4_hWZlICep0w263pqZuloO7AW3Uhtohbfv7RdTFJ2nVU-c_GqqISwXGJhjsNvBs2x6HHfUkC202RLwd3iaa3QjJUMVq1336eETu4fBWp1cSgyWBDFfJnCMHH6mO4ssMJ2WLr3NJH2AUaA-YAABE8M6gzC8vs8_Vf282wi-tGOMJQIkefi3s7cDfPLj2NKdTOu8sS3bZZhbvfBTZtF8BDHjAoCI54DJfr44pCdbfLppuiun-48bJzwqguKL_QkLnEtmVDPZhjrdKKVpi7gwL_uRzYUHh0lHaQ.jpg","video":"","hasVideo":false},{"id":"479","date":"2026-11-12T22:35:36+00:00","text":"Wet Dress Rehearsal complete ✅ Electron is ready for its 100th launch this weekend from Launch Complex 1. 'The Mountain God Rises' launch window opens tomorrow Nov 14: 🚀 6:30pm NZDT 🚀 2:30 pm JST 🚀 05:30 UTC 🚀 12:30 am ET 🚀 9:30 pm PT (Nov 13)","image":"","video":"https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/05480d34fc.mp4?token=NUGSPqfUE-dLJxQEct3_J2zl5cwjv1JrThzzta_O-QDoXy7pAbuQrv-_zpHMm1ozcdvQFrhR-07RlqsE71XmaozvAol3asocUwXXIClDusJYtXzszfET882d5ryCSNgsuUFX6nJ5lKL00iUZRzzZq5c-rfGgMj5HNlC-dzihCYSc4pFuAZOODxM3sL8EFms8ufwQwDIT8f15-4p6_BCxfwajF_kM_8Ul38AlLT11BhIuMkixLLqTD11O8XCl6KAQMyCkFRadM_WbWscqWZBAYD-3pxBJfzzyZ7zUXcsMjXc6q_RyABMacSDj6QMyEouNbbTUqcGFVueBPEgK8EyTDmW9RRi0P5FnIQCTLSR_6RZfU454yZ-vG-1cYnCqVfWrIr95PKXgUvdBmadaiUYE5Qu-kuki3ALGH1h2p6q2Cwo2v-owTXCAEpyqNFnpUV30Zbu7fMsL2uWtwrViI1dtG5sKrc9bIZ195eilDNpqraCWjjkDELfSQ3SMq1fbYwndk5aEP4nvEOEAtbx8VzT4FVJKeI-kbk_4aNLnFdhU2sqkwHKSBnidn1mwTMb7ijez_4qZsnLAWPkNGQAUPUBS-D8pjNPeNPhCbp21fEq4F-Yajc-PYkFF1-YvFpWxM7AwqDkaGI5wtjsut4mtbp-JE_OL5AxFH2im3w1-snlXr5E","hasVideo":true},{"id":"475","date":"2026-11-11T22:00:44+00:00","text":"100 launches, one incredible team. We couldn't be prouder of the people who are making it possible with sheer determination, late nights, problem solving under pressure, and by showing up for each other for every single mission.","image":"https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/Peh2tCuyOushIzG5aQzr2z_jUoU2EbqxK0WComnVcVmduDgaOioi_od7px7ic3XPCP4lvSAlKUPQ1tKaeQhvlEN34YEh4j2FjFbyvelS9h1-cqvHtFlbJBYCe_zG7JyV9ddac3Vy9K7Pu-44ZWHtekqCf8P8YY9mr3Njh7zJAI-pVWd9aymukCBMA4W2fNvkPdZw8NBLwT4gFYKcrihYcZyuu_gm8ssFHbQ0ndzXeWVwcRG15n9i7P0QyyprKfieftF5nZeYVi9jVbFEgfHLHp8ivF74G3BFRo_BnmRwcMsSqb9RiLvHNe9lxIFtIBss6EzLKNrLiZFs84P0UAwyGQ.jpg","video":"","hasVideo":false},{"id":"474","date":"2026-11-11T21:24:31+00:00","text":"Today we honor the veterans who have served, including the many who now help build the future of space at Rocket Lab. Thank you and Happy Veterans Day.","image":"https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/HeM_X5esB8N6xr8upg-ITVw9hQ4ge589R9xPYXutpLufqKo39QyWcvy-wJ7G1VcpvLy8kAFMOgv4L_ikMgvz4wFW316P_VAkI221kfYZHg9k2lYVkKlsEmcl83xDEOSwPn5pDAIZYGm35naxliyEpmnj33f7MPX3MlE1kpyg6RMZf-MNrIMx-tsYKPLYzPDxBtdE0lYpepJSqHU4YUAF72VLXK-09qRMSkUq3D7bd7TLIxBLJeuhhISk5iY7Fg26yzCQag1rjFg_54H3H8YCAPBkpkvidHsBjfHNP_m7YXS-NqvB78GSS2hPlSiBgVBupZLtYvyieI7kPny0f1I3NQ.jpg","video":"","hasVideo":false},{"id":"473","date":"2026-11-11T04:09:10+00:00","text":"Our spacecraft just made interplanetary history - twice. Blue & Gold flawlessly executed powered Earth gravity assists, two days apart, to slingshot our planet and shoot for Mars' orbit. This is the first time the highly complex maneuver has been executed successfully by spacecraft. ESCAPADE has proven a new path is possible to make it to Mars outside the typical Earth-to-Mars launch window that occurs every 26 months. Next ESCAPADE mission milestone: Mars Orbit Insertion, September 2027.","image":"","video":"","hasVideo":false}]
